# RLHF-style three-objective bandit with prompt-distribution shift.
# Pre-shift the prompts come mostly from cluster 0 (e.g., factual Q&A),
# post-shift mostly from cluster K-1 (e.g., creative writing). Different
# arms are optimal for different clusters, so an algorithm that doesn't
# adapt loses on all three objectives simultaneously.
#
# This is the headline RLHF benchmark — closest to what production
# RLHF deployments actually face (training distribution != deployment
# distribution).

name: rlhf_prompt_shift
description: |
  Three-objective RLHF benchmark with single prompt-distribution shift.
  Mirrors the production RLHF deployment problem where the training
  distribution differs from the deployment distribution. Tests whether
  PCBShift's d_p-aware adaptation transfers to M=3.
horizon: 10000
n_seeds: 20
delta: 0.05

environment:
  type: RLHFBandit
  n_arms: 4
  embedding_dim: 4
  n_clusters: 3
  schedule: single
  shift_times: [5000]
  sigma: 0.05

algorithms:
algorithms:
  - PCBShift
  - Auer16
  - ParetoUCB
  - AnnealingPareto
  - Kone23
  - Cai24
  - ScalarizedUCB
  - RandomPlay

metrics:
  - PreferenceRegret
  - HausdorffRegret
  - DominanceCoverage
  - ParetoPrecisionRecall
